-- title:
--   Norm compatibility of the order-4 and order-8 Artin ray symbols
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, equipped with a group isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$, and let $\zeta \in \mathbb{C}$ satisfy $\zeta^4 = -1$. Write $K''$ for the fixed field of `c4H e`, the subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ generated by the integral powers of $(\mathtt{gammaT } e)^2$, where $\mathtt{gammaT } e = e^{-1}(\mathtt{tbarGL})$, and $K'$ for the fixed field of `c8H e`, the subgroup of those $\gamma$ whose image $e(\gamma)$ is the entrywise reduction `red` of some matrix in `C8`. Let $I$ be a non-zero ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{K''}$ such that for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_{K''}$ occurring with non-zero multiplicity `FractionalIdeal.count` in $I$, the chosen prime `primeAbove` of $\mathcal{O}_L$ above $w$ has trivial inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$. Then the ray symbol of $I$ over $K''$ for the prime-value function `artinValue4 e hζ`, that is the locally finite product $\prod_{w} (\mathtt{artinValue4 } e\, h\zeta\ w)^{\mathrm{ord}_w(I)}$ of values of the character `chiGal4 e hζ` (the restriction of `chiGal e hζ` to `c4H e`) at the seed Frobenius elements `seedFrob (c4H e) w`, equals the corresponding ray symbol over $K'$ for `artinValue e hζ` evaluated at the relative norm `Ideal.relNorm` of $I$ down to $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$, both ideals being read as fractional ideals.
--
--   This is norm-functoriality of the Artin symbol, in ideal-theoretic form, for the quadratic step $K''/K'$ inside the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$-extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$: the order-4 ray symbol on ideals of $\mathcal{O}_{K''}$ is the order-8 ray symbol of the relative norm, the prime-by-prime input being the relation between `artinValue4` and `artinValue` at primes with trivial inertia together with $N_{K''/K'}(w) = (w \cap \mathcal{O}_{K'})^{f}$ with $f$ the residue degree. It is used in the construction of the quadratic ray class character attached to the $C_8$-data, in the step producing the trace-seed table for the quaternion subgroup.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_P2_raySymbol_artinValue4_eq_raySymbol_artinValue_relNorm_of_inertia_rat.lean

